  "findings": [
    "The fixed current64 tracked Archive inputs are a separate diagnostic census, including .gitignore and exact fixture/reference bytes. They are not substituted for the older62-file proof scope. Three shared host inputs plus three diagnostic files yield70 captured sources, each authenticated to actual committed Git and checked before execution and independently afterward.",
    "Only the two unchanged original app.integration.test.mjs and app.test.mjs files run, with all five original groups selected. The collector authenticates clean hosted Windows/X64/Node24.16.0, exact job and actual HEAD, prohibits inherited NODE_OPTIONS, and retains raw stdout/stderr before parsing. The five-minute whole-diagnostic boundary leaves the original native15-second deadline and every original test assertion unchanged.",
    "The hook authenticates the exact source-metadata.mjs bytes and derives its literal original UTF16LE encoded script as data. Selection requires the exact native executable, original encoded command and original options. Every other execFile call forwards untouched. syncBuiltinESMExports exposes the wrapper to the original named ESM import.",
    "For selected native calls, the wrapper forwards the original executable, argument array, option object, receiver and resulting ChildProcess. Its callback forwards the original error/stdout/stderr/receiver after recording. Trace retention errors fail diagnostic observability while still forwarding the product callback. No stdin, arguments, output contents or error.message are recorded; retained observations contain fixed provenance, PID/sequence, elapsed time, code/killed/signal and byte counts.",
    "The workflow always attempts the separate source postcheck and bounded packaging after failures. Complete artifacts remain below the existing96-member/16MiBraw/8MiBZIP bounds; overflow produces a clearly incomplete failed fallback. Actions are pinned, permissions are read-only and no paid resource or original vendor asset is acquired.",
    "The source declares instrumentedDependencyObserver and diagnosticOnly. A fresh observed native error belongs only to this new diagnostic attempt. Hook loading and trace writes add observation overhead, so this is not an uninstrumented performance comparison or a full1100-suite rerun. The earlier d24 native cause remains unobserved."
  ],
  "remainingAcceptance": "After root copies and commits these exact inert sources, only the verified hosted workflow may execute them. Preserve and independently authenticate actual raw API/logs, all uploaded bytes, two selected workers' observations, source-before/after and packaging scope before reporting a diagnostic result. A failed or incomplete diagnostic must stay failed; no prior receipt, product source or deadline may be rebound.",
